PROBE 1 (KEPT, byte-exact on the FIRST probe). Replaced the goto-join body of FindWORLDOBJ with a helper defined immediately before it:

static inline WorldObj* sFindWorldObj(WorldObj* node, char* name) {
    s16 index;

    while (node != 0) {
        if (strcmp(name, node->desc) == 0) {
            return node;
        }
        index = node->childidx;
        if (index >= 0) {
            WorldObj* r = FindWorldObject(&world_objects[index], name);
            if (r != 0) {
                return r;
            }
        }
        index = node->nextidx;
        if (index >= 0) {
            node = &world_objects[index];
        } else {
            return 0;
        }
    }
    return 0;
}

WorldObj* FindWORLDOBJ(char* name) {
    return sFindWorldObj(world_objects, name);
}

The `static inline` keyword is LOAD-BEARING and was added as a second step: with a plain `static` helper the object bytes of FindWORLDOBJ were already exact, but MWCC ALSO emitted a standalone sFindWorldObj body, and its exception record cost the TU 144 bytes of matched Data image-wide (ninja PROGRESS Data 177572 -> 177428, Game Code Data 66.06% -> 65.92%). With `static inline` the standalone body is not emitted, defake_gate stops reporting a NEW function, and Data returns to 177572 / 7.52%.
